        "original_id": "b50d9efa-5620-557d-9e25-bce370376a75",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Woo, Joseph Santley, Ti Lung, Leslie Cheung, Chow Yun-fat\n- Films: A Better Tomorrow, City on Fire\n- Roles: film director, writer, producer, actor, singer, dancer\n- Places: Hong Kong, China, Asia, North America\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph Santley was born as Joseph Ishmael Mansfield on January 10, 1890, and he became an American actor, singer, dancer, writer, director, and producer of musical theatrical plays, motion pictures, and television shows.\n- John Woo SBS, also known as Ng Yu-Sum, was born on May 1, 1946, and he is a Chinese-born Hong Kong film director, writer, and producer.\n- A Better Tomorrow is a 1986 Hong Kong crime film directed by John Woo and starring Ti Lung, Leslie Cheung, and Chow Yun-fat.\n- Following A Better Tomorrow in 1986, the 1987 film City on Fire helped establish Chow Yun-fat's popularity as an action star in Asia and, to a lesser degree, North America.\n- Joseph Santley died on August 8, 1971.",
